    {
      "id": "claim_30cd17b589aa4d6dbd27a0d5fff2c5ca",
      "statement": "Guards are server-side rules that block requests based on conditions. The consents gate uses a guard rule that blocks authenticated users who haven't accepted current Terms/Privacy Policy, returns HTTP 451, excludes anonymous callers/auth endpoints/acceptance request, and importantly does not exclude /users/me to make the gate work without client-side probing.",
